# r102 (2026-11-11, s90): the r101 window pinned the r94 wall to launchd's
# AccessoryInteraction aborting pid 1 at the first MKBGetDeviceLockState
# failure -- on this no-SEP board nothing answers the unchanged
# libaks/MobileKeyBag AppleKeyStore state queries (the same situation the
# upstream sirius/sheng records document; sheng enables the answer service
# with aks=1). This row is the m2381 keystore-face fork of the arch
# series' offline-legacy-start.patch: the hook site is already patched into
# the tree by that row, so this patch retargets the compile-time gate so
# XNU_NATIVE_KEYSTORE wires ONLY the AppleKeyStore stand-in publication
# (device package KeyStoreProbe.cpp + the AppleKeyStoreState component's
# NativeKeyStoreEvents user client, both upstream-proven on sheng hardware)
# while the display late probe keeps its own XNU_NATIVE_LEGACY_DISPLAY gate
# and stays compiled out on this donor-kext display lane. All three gates
# are boot-arg self-gated (offline-keystore/offline-key-events/aks),
# so the row is inert without the board.toml args even when compiled in.
offline-keystore-start.patch
